{{smaller block|The firste thousand, that is of Dukes, of Erles, of Marquyses and of Amyralles, alle clothed in Clothes of Gold, with ''Tysseux'' of grene Silk.
{{right|''Mandeville'', Travels, p. 233.}}}}

{{smaller block|The vpper garment of the stately Queen
Is rich gold ''Tissue'', on a ground of green.
{{right|''Sylvester'', tr. of Du Bartas's Weeks, ii., The Decay.}}}}

{{smaller block|His skill in the judgment of rich ''tissues'' . . . is exceeding.
{{right|''J. F. Cooper'', Water-Witch, xxvii.}}}}
